{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-008",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 8,
  "title": "Job 8",
  "display_title": "Job 8",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 8,
  "sortOrder": 18008,
  "verseCount": 22,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then answered Bildad the Shuhite, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "How long wilt thou speak these things? and how long shall the words of thy mouth be like a strong wind?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Doth God pervert judgment? or doth the Almighty pervert justice?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "If thy children have sinned against him, and he have cast them away for their transgression;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "If thou wouldest seek unto God betimes, and make thy supplication to the Almighty;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "If thou wert pure and upright; surely now he would awake for thee, and make the habitation of thy righteousness prosperous.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Though thy beginning was small, yet thy latter end should greatly increase.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "For enquire, I pray thee, of the former age, and prepare thyself to the search of their fathers:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "(For we are but of yesterday, and know nothing, because our days upon earth are a shadow:)",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Shall not they teach thee, and tell thee, and utter words out of their heart?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Can the rush grow up without mire? can the flag grow without water?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Whilst it is yet in his greenness, and not cut down, it withereth before any other herb.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "So are the paths of all that forget God; and the hypocrite’s hope shall perish:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Whose hope shall be cut off, and whose trust shall be a spider’s web.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "He shall lean upon his house, but it shall not stand: he shall hold it fast, but it shall not endure.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "He is green before the sun, and his branch shooteth forth in his garden.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "His roots are wrapped about the heap, and seeth the place of stones.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "If he destroy him from his place, then it shall deny him, saying, I have not seen thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Behold, this is the joy of his way, and out of the earth shall others grow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Behold, God will not cast away a perfect man, neither will he help the evil doers:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "Till he fill thy mouth with laughing, and thy lips with rejoicing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:8:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "They that hate thee shall be clothed with shame; and the dwelling place of the wicked shall come to nought.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 8:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:8:22"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
